[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49664"] :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)]+[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0]+[0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-114328/selection/cb4e5ec82e27c1b1c72f308818d951f3f6df262d558af5bf66b95e1ff52f9a1c" :answer/id #uuid "145f1c58-cfee-5fbf-bb6a-b2d26ce59f7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114328/selection/7a4972d114a919ef0b73f5547b321b46f940a627930ce1bf682b990a70159f93" :answer/id #uuid "6665f252-6c4e-5063-be8d-6597716207c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114328/selection/140d02b77bda7ff1bfd7cf4aa201328912415a59741e456c4856a76c4c25b7e0" :answer/id #uuid "e0bfe633-9542-5635-b9f5-65048e44510d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114328/selection/645ed9dc55431673d827e07ccb98a0069163faf0b35ce131518cf9cc56c3394f" :answer/id #uuid "f684ea8c-12be-51a8-848f-81d34460df2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114328/selection/a6d640f49c26b91dbfd91278a4c1169a5f7550648294738e81e3daf8c35b6023" :answer/id #uuid "47cf9938-640b-58c9-a257-ee079f7dbf1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114328/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f523db39-2d52-5658-9cf0-7d10756bc93d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114328/selection/7a4972d114a919ef0b73f5547b321b46f940a627930ce1bf682b990a70159f93" :answer-field/choices ["q-114328/selection/cb4e5ec82e27c1b1c72f308818d951f3f6df262d558af5bf66b95e1ff52f9a1c" "q-114328/selection/7a4972d114a919ef0b73f5547b321b46f940a627930ce1bf682b990a70159f93" "q-114328/selection/140d02b77bda7ff1bfd7cf4aa201328912415a59741e456c4856a76c4c25b7e0" "q-114328/selection/645ed9dc55431673d827e07ccb98a0069163faf0b35ce131518cf9cc56c3394f" "q-114328/selection/a6d640f49c26b91dbfd91278a4c1169a5f7550648294738e81e3daf8c35b6023"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114328" :question/id #uuid "30055505-3f80-5aa5-bd67-0ffdf3305263" :question/math-academy-id "q-114328" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{9}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)+\\frac{1}{9}(0-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114328/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114328"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
